1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,304
Gamma is always bigger than one, so the adiabatic is gamma times steeper at every point.

2
00:00:07,304 --> 00:00:11,796
Turn gamma down towards one, and the two curves merge.

3
00:00:11,796 --> 00:00:19,192
Turn it up to one point six seven, for a monatomic gas, and the adiabatic falls even more steeply.

